{"diagnosis": "Loopback sent 0xa5 but reg_dat_do returned 0x25 (0xa5 & 0x7F, MSB cleared). recv_buf_data is declared as reg [7:1] on line 42, a 7-bit vector, so an 8-bit receive pattern loses bit[7] on assignment and zero-extends on read via line 53. Widening to [7:0] preserves the full byte.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@
 	reg [3:0] recv_state;
 	reg [31:0] recv_divcnt;
 	reg [7:0] recv_pattern;
-	reg [7:1] recv_buf_data;
+	reg [7:0] recv_buf_data;
 	reg recv_buf_valid;

 	reg [9:0] send_pattern;", "expected": "tohost: PASS, uart data match got 0xa5 want 0xa5 with no TRAP"}

